      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Object Storage Tasks**\n\nI'm currently focused on defining the initial Python files for managed object storage. The first is `upload_object.py`, where the user specified using an external provider like Microsoft/OpenAI. Considering this is an object storage task, I should choose Azure.\n\n\n**Outlining Object Storage Functions**\n\nI've sketched a plan for ten Python files for managed object storage, prioritizing `upload_object.py` with Azure Blob Storage. Helper files like `storage_models.py` and `storage_client.py` will come first. I aim for modularity, starting with core object storage tasks before moving to AI/ML integrations for OCR and translation. I will focus on `upload_object.py`, `presigned_download.py`, `object_metadata.py`, and `list_prefix.py` utilizing the Azure Blob Storage.\n\n\n**Prioritizing File Development**\n\nI'm now diving into the specifics of file implementation. `storage_models.py` and `storage_client.py` are underway as foundational helpers for Azure Blob Storage interaction, with definitions for data models and client initialization, respectively. Then, I will address `upload_object.py`. I'm going to follow the same-scenario files first, such as `presigned_download.py`, `object_metadata.py`, and `list_prefix.py`. After that, I will work on the later-step files like those involving OCR and translation, and lastly, the OpenAI implementations.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789896109452,
          "start": 1789896105659
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
